<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-HIAP MOH 1H PROFIT DOWN 57.5 PCT.</title>
<headline>TABLE-HIAP MOH 1H PROFIT DOWN 57.5 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			 (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   0.47    vs    1.10</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		  0.16    vs    0.37</p>
<p>    Turnover			    21.03    vs   13.50</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		 0.39    vs    0.37</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation  0.85    vs    0.78</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     0.15    vs    1.57</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	  0.90    vs     nil</p>
<p>    Tax				    0.58    vs    0.46</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		    0.57    vs   (0.14)</p>
<p>Note - Hiap Moh Corp Ltd makes and trade paper products. It said that in view of the continued decline in the demand for commodity paper, it did not expect any improvement in its core business for the second half year ending December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
